A. Business-Service Check Status Transaction Flow

1. Create a crone job in the transaction_status table and check Txn_Status_Initial where status in PENDING_TIMEOUT and PENDING_THIRD_PARTY
	i. If status is PENDING_TIMEOUT
		a. Send transaction to Kafka topic
		b. If Kafka fails:
			i. Log and CONTINUE to the next transaction
		c. Otherwise, 
			1. Listen for transactions response from Technical-Service on a Kafka Topic
			2. On a different thread, Update DB:
				i.   Update DB Txn_Status_Initial & Txn_Status_Final: <SUCCESS, FAILURE, or PENDING_THIRD_PARTY>
				ii.  Update DB Txn_Status_Final_Desc: <Give desc>
			3. Log and CONTINUE to the next transaction	
				
	ii. If status is PENDING_THIRD_PARTY
		a. Call Technical Service's Status Check sycn API via Eureka Registry 
		b. Update DB Txn_Status_Initial & Txn_Status_Final: <SUCCESS, FAILURE, or PENDING_THIRD_PARTY>
		c. Update DB Txn_Status_Final_Desc: <Give desc>
		d. Log and CONTINUE to the next transaction

